# File Operations

**Applies to**: All file creation, modification, reading, and searching

## Commands

| Action | Correct | Wrong |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Create file | Write tool | `echo "..." > file`, `cat << EOF > file` |
| Edit file | Edit tool | `sed -i`, `awk`, bash heredoc |
| Read file | Read tool | `cat file`, `head`, `tail` |
| Find files | Glob tool | `find . -name`, `ls -R` |
| Search content | Grep tool | `grep`, `rg` via bash |

## Why

Write/Edit tools execute without user permission. Bash file operations require individual approval, blocking autonomous execution.

## Exception

Bash is correct for: git operations, running tests (`uv run pytest`, `yarn test`), installing packages (`uv add`, `yarn add`), starting servers.
